The Nutrition Assistant system is structured as a clear distributed system divided into three main operational blocks:

1. User Interface (Frontend)
   - Built using React.js and styled modern components.
   - Represents the interface through which users interact with the system, enter fitness metrics, and view macro targets.

2. Backend Services (Server Logic)
   - Built on Node.js and Express.js.
   - Includes custom API routes for handling client requests and responses securely.
   - Houses the core Nutrition Functions module that handles calculations for BMI, BMR, and daily calorie breakdowns.

3. Database Layer (Storage)
   - Powering data persistence via MongoDB using Mongoose schemas.
   - Responsibly handles storing user authentication credentials and logs historical diet suggestions chronologically.

4. External Services
   - Flexible integration capabilities for external nutritional databases or food tracking APIs to dynamically reference menu ingredients.
